---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { OWNER, SITE_NAME, withBase } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description={`${SITE_NAME} is a curated directory. We do not take payment for rankings. Listings are written from official specs.`}
  canonicalPath="about"
>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <p class="kicker">About this directory</p>
    <h1>We curate. We don’t sell the ranking.</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a public, slow-growing directory of robot lawn mowers — wire-free LiDAR, RTK,
      and vision models as well as boundary-wire machines. It is run by {OWNER}.
      The homepage is the index. Each listing is one Markdown file, one page, one set of facts.
    </p>

    <h2>What “curated” means here</h2>
    <p>
      New models are added because they ship, not because a brand paid. There is no sponsored
      ranking, no “best of 2026” package, and no invented testimonials. If that policy changes,
      this page will say so first.
    </p>

    <h2>How a listing is written</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Official product pages and spec sheets are the source of truth.</li>
      <li>If a number is not on that page, it is omitted rather than guessed.</li>
      <li>Prices are labeled with a note (MSRP vs live cart vs unknown).</li>
      <li>The verdict is a caveat-aware one-liner, not a marketing sentence.</li>
      <li>Pages are updated when new hardware ships or official specs change.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Coverage, slope, and navigation</h2>
    <p>
      Coverage is the manufacturer’s recommended mowing area, not a promise that every yard of
      that size will finish in one charge. Slope is the published maximum inside the work area
      unless noted. Navigation tags (LiDAR, RTK, vision, boundary wire) describe what the maker
      claims the mower uses — mixed systems get more than one tag.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on this site may be affiliate links. Seed listings ship with empty affiliate
      URLs. When a link is an affiliate, the footer disclosure still applies: some links may be
      affiliate. That does not change the spec table.
    </p>

    <p><a href={withBase()}>Back to the directory</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
